{
  "id": "ss.proj.bolt",
  "name": "Acid glob",
  "description": "A mouthful of acid in flight \u2014 round and heavy at the front where the air holds it, drawn out to a thread behind, and nothing else: no shed beads, no debris. Two things keep it off the Gland's bolt, which is the other spit on this screen: it runs bile \u2014 venom pulled toward gold until it reads acidic rather than merely green \u2014 where that one is spore teal, and it has a tail where that one is a closed lozenge. Either separator alone would fail on a busy screen; together they hold. The wet read comes from one hard white gloss high on the head \u2014 that single dot is the difference between a liquid and a painted ball. Points +x, which is the direction the weapon code rotates it to. The id stays `bolt` because the game maps it by id; the drawing is what changed.",
