  "variants": {
    "evolved": {
      "description": "The evolved glob: pale bile with something set hard at the centre \u2014 a dark seed with a cut face, carried inside the drop rather than stuck on the front. The rest of the drawing is a viscous thing coming apart under its own flight: the head is an ellipse pressed taller than it is wide by the air, the mass necks down behind it, and only past that neck does it tear into three ribbons of unequal length and weight. Both halves of that matter. A drop that split at the head read as a creature with limbs, and strands drawn thin enough to be even read as wire rather than liquid \u2014 this has to look like something that is about to let go, which is exactly what it does: the first thing it lands on breaks it and it comes apart into six. That texture is the only one the splatter has, so those six drops are this same image at a little over half size, and the seed has to still read as a seed there. It never grows a spike; a point drawn on the front turned it into a leaf.",
